        "citations": null,
        "text": "There are **three ways** to change a `<span>`'s color on mouse over. Here they are, from simplest to most advanced:\n\n---\n\n## \u2705 Method 1: CSS `:hover` Pseudo-class (Recommended)\n\nThis is the simplest and cleanest approach.\n\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n  <head>\n    <style>\n      span {\n        color: black;\n        cursor: pointer;\n      }\n\n      span:hover {\n        color: red;\n      }\n    </style>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <span>Hover over me!</span>\n  </body>\n</html>\n```\n\n",
        "type": "text"
      },
