      {
        "citations": null,
        "text": "\n\n---\n\n## \u2705 Method 3: External JavaScript with `addEventListener`\n\nThis is the most flexible and scalable approach for larger projects:\n\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n  <body>\n    <span id=\"mySpan\">Hover over me!</span>\n\n    <script>\n      const span = document.getElementById(\"mySpan\");\n\n      span.addEventListener(\"mouseover\", function () {\n        this.style.color = \"red\";\n      });\n\n      span.addEventListener(\"mouseout\", function () {\n        this.style.color = \"black\";\n      });\n    </script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n```\n\n",
